 and now; it just allowed Lunars to emulate Breeding in order to buoy up the Dragon-Blooded generationally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T00:49:25-07:00","id":1449519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1448390-lunar-charm-awakens-dragon-blooded-lineage-2nd-ed?p=1449488#post1449488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the closest thing was in Ink Monkeys? But it didn't really work for individuals in the here and now; it just allowed Lunars to emulate Breeding in order to buoy up the Dragon-Blooded generationally.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that context I think I know what it was.<br /> I recall Shomshak initially had a Lunar charm as part of Dzibilch\u00e1n that meant them having higher essence didn't automatically create Moonborn and gave them phantom Breeding dots but ultimately changed it to a deal with Parad, the God of Inherited Might rather than a rape charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud